    "created_at": "2023-02-28T17:35:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-02-28T17:35:06Z",
    "body": "For developing FLEDGE [0], we'd be interested in enums that don't throw, since we have several \"enums\" that will grow as we add new functionality. Often, feature detection seems like it needn't be necessary, since ignoring unsupported enum fields on older browsers seems sufficient for our use-cases? \r\n\r\nFor now, due to this issue, we're using strings instead of enums.\r\n\r\n[0] https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/blob/main/FLEDGE.md",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
