    "created_at": "2023-06-05T15:04:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-05T15:04:32Z",
    "body": "For integers we have `Clamp` and `EnforceRange` extended attributes to control throwing or changing the value. If specs want to use enums but not throw it seems useful to add an extended attribute to opt in to no throwing. Should it only work when setting a default value, where unknown values are converted to the default value?",
